1
00:00:00,572 --> 00:00:03,802
(Mary:)and I, for one, am thrilled.

2
00:00:05,343 --> 00:00:06,973
(Sheldon:)What?

3
00:00:06,978 --> 00:00:09,848
What... Where's the judgment?

4
00:00:09,848 --> 00:00:12,478
W-Where's the fire
and brimstone?

5
00:00:12,483 --> 00:00:14,613
(Sheldon:)Where's the part where you tell
us we're going to Hell

6
00:00:14,619 --> 00:00:16,119
(Sheldon:)and I say have you seen
the size of the bugs outside?

7
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,290
We're already there!

8
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:21,620
(Mary:)Obviously, I would prefer if you
weren't living out of wedlock,

9
00:00:21,626 --> 00:00:23,896
(Mary:)but given
your special circumstances,

10
00:00:23,895 --> 00:00:26,925
(Mary:)I'm very happy for you.

11
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:33,106
And what "special circumstances"
are those?

12
00:00:33,104 --> 00:00:36,004
(Penny:)Oh, boy, I think it's
about to get bad.

13
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:39,508
(Mary:)Shelly, how do I put this?

14
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:42,140
(Mary:)By your third birthday,
you had memorized

15
00:00:42,146 --> 00:00:45,186
(Mary:)over a thousand different kinds
of trains,

16
00:00:45,183 --> 00:00:47,453
(Mary:)and I never imagined

17
00:00:47,452 --> 00:00:51,852
(Mary:)a woman getting aboard
any of them.

18
00:00:54,726 --> 00:00:57,926
(Sheldon:)What, so... You thought
I was going to be alone

19
00:00:57,929 --> 00:00:59,729
(Sheldon:)for the rest of my life?

20
00:00:59,731 --> 00:01:03,021
No! Just for the middle part.

